## Upgrading a Master to 3008.x
> :warning: **Reminder**: <br>
If your master is being upgraded from 3006.x/3007.x, see the
[3008.0 release notes](3008.0.md#minion-data-cache-reorganized-refresh-grains-after-upgrading-the-master)
about the minion data cache reorganization — run
``salt '*' saltutil.refresh_grains`` on minions after the upgrade.

## Master Cluster: Node Identity Changed — Migration Required
> :warning: **Upgrade Notice (clustered masters only)**: <br>
[#70568](https://github.com/saltstack/salt/pull/70568) fixes
[#70567](https://github.com/saltstack/salt/issues/70567) by changing the
cluster-wide node identity from ``opts["interface"]`` to ``opts["id"]``
(with the ``_master`` suffix stripped). This is required so founding-voter
election and peer handshakes work when masters bind to ``0.0.0.0`` / ``::``
or when ``cluster_peers`` is specified by hostname rather than by IP.
>
> **Who is affected**: existing 3008.0–3008.2 clustered masters whose
> ``opts["interface"]`` differs from their ``opts["id"]`` (the common
> case — ``interface`` is typically an IP, ``id`` typically a hostname).
> Standalone (non-clustered) masters are not affected.
>
> **What changes on-disk**:
> - Raft storage path moves from
>   ``<cachedir>/cluster/consensus/<interface>/log`` to
>   ``<cachedir>/cluster/consensus/<node_id>/log``.
> - The cluster-join sentinel moves from
>   ``<cachedir>/.cluster_joined.<interface>`` to
>   ``<cachedir>/.cluster_joined.<node_id>``.
> - Peer pubkey files under ``<cluster_pki_dir>/peers/`` are now looked up
>   by ``<node_id>.pub`` instead of ``<interface>.pub``.
>
> **Before upgrading**:
> 1. On every master in the cluster, set :conf_master:`id` explicitly and
>    make sure each master's ``id`` matches the name its siblings list in
>    their ``cluster_peers``. See the updated
>    [master cluster tutorial](../tutorials/master-cluster) for details.
> 2. Rename each master's ``<cluster_pki_dir>/peers/<old-interface>.pub``
>    to ``<cluster_pki_dir>/peers/<new-node-id>.pub`` on every master.
>
> **On upgrade**: the Raft log at the old path is not read; the cluster
> will re-bootstrap under the new identity (lowest ``node_id`` founds,
> others join as learners). Expect a short window during which the cluster
> re-forms before resuming normal operation.

